{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{U_j \\to X\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-dominates-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a3b52269a0c00952d5937f7a87d489753761493b7458412b477818f3115d42f0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a5f19a6a842d7bdf734a3aa8523e049c2ec1cf109a2d914e29139495282dbaa8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a smooth covering of <MATH_0005>.\nThen there exists an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering <MATH_0006>\nof <MATH_0007> which refines <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c0041b037e05a24325c80a9722eecff5b25db8793a7e217128e735ce4dbd48c4", "unit_id": "tag:0CFV:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$i$", "MATH_0004": "$W_i$", "MATH_0005": "$W_i \\to X_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{W_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{W_i \\times_X U \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{U_j \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{W_i \\times_X U \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{U_j \\to X\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-etale-dominates-smooth}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c6a61e936be55b46a5b3d0e5f6fdf9bb6113c4a4e0315cf62ebb9b5d08244412", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:41e9d89ee7c768ba009c6e7a40383f870cc89db39cfc75823cf710d067148b72", "source_text": "First choose a scheme <MATH_0001> and a surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0002>.\nFor each <MATH_0003> choose a scheme <MATH_0004> and a surjective <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism\n<MATH_0005>. Then <MATH_0006> is a smooth covering\nwhich refines <MATH_0007>. Hence\n<MATH_0008> is a smooth covering of schemes.\nBy More on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe can choose an <ACCENT_0003>tale covering <MATH_0009> which refines\n<MATH_0010>. Then <MATH_0011>\nis an <ACCENT_0004>tale covering refining <MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d115270805d7a79247c8b57ea041adf31470b4adc3a881d15286f0aa4e362627", "unit_id": "tag:0CFV:proof"}
